    "result_text": "All 271 tests pass \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS, no regressions.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change makes telephone numbers store as digits-only and normalize before the uniqueness check. Three coordinated edits:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 relaxed the `OwnerFields.telephone` regex from `^[0-9]*$` to `^[0-9()\\s-]*$` so punctuated input like `(613) 555-0100` passes bean validation instead of being rejected with a 400. (The DTO is regenerated from this spec at build time.)\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 `setTelephone` now strips every non-digit (`replaceAll(\"[^0-9]\", \"\")`, null-safe), so the persisted/returned value is canonical digits. This is the single source of truth covering both create (via the MapStruct mapper) and update (via `ApplyOwner`); DB loads use field access and are unaffected.\n\n3. **`rest/function/owner/EnsureOwnerUnique.java`** \u2014 `normalize` now strips to digits so the uniqueness comparison treats `(613) 555-0100` and `6135550100` as the same number, satisfying \"apply this normalization before the telephone-uniqueness check.\"\n\nThe two new `Cp11Tests` (stores digits-only; normalized duplicate rejected with 409) pass, and the entire suite of 271 tests stays green \u2014 including the existing owner controller tests where non-punctuation garbage (letters) is still rejected as before.",
